WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.386 --> 00:00:16.448
and Kaa finally reached the edge of Monkey City.

2
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:21.310
They could see Mowgli in a circle with monkeys surrounding him.

3
00:00:22.611 --> 00:00:24.612
The two friends slipped into a ditch.

4
00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:29.415
"I wish Baloo was here," Bagheera whispered.

5
00:00:29.435 --> 00:00:31.736
"But we will do what we can."

6
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.481
He looked up at the sky.

7
00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:39.023
"When that cloud covers the moon, I'll go to the terrace."

8
00:00:39.043 --> 00:00:42.044
"Good luck," Kaa whispered.

9
00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:45.385
"I will go over the west wall."

10
00:00:46.726 --> 00:00:48.127
Then he glided away.

11
00:00:49.647 --> 00:00:52.629
The monkeys were still giving boastful speeches.

12
00:00:53.749 --> 00:00:55.550
Mowgli saw it was getting dark.

13
00:00:58.311 --> 00:01:03.046
Suddenly he heard something—Bagheera's light feet on the marble terrace.

14
00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:04.988
"It worked!"

15
00:01:05.488 --> 00:01:06.609
he thought with relief.

16
00:01:06.629 --> 00:01:08.871
"My plan worked!"

17
00:01:10.813 --> 00:01:13.995
With a furious roar, the panther rushed forward.

18
00:01:15.977 --> 00:01:18.699
He darted right and left, striking monkeys.

19
00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.283
The startled creatures howled with fright and rage.

20
00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:27.086
Finally a monkey managed to kick Bagheera.

21
00:01:27.106 --> 00:01:29.568
"There's only one attacker!"

22
00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:30.693
she shouted.

23
00:01:30.713 --> 00:01:32.614
"Let's get him!"

24
00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.917
A mass of monkeys surrounded Bagheera.

25
00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:40.741
They were biting, scratching, tearing, and pulling.

26
00:01:42.002 --> 00:01:44.744
Meanwhile another group had grabbed Mowgli.

27
00:01:45.925 --> 00:01:48.207
They dragged him up the wall of a temple.

28
00:01:50.328 --> 00:01:53.591
Then they pushed him through a hole in its broken dome.

29
00:01:55.152 --> 00:01:59.536
A boy raised by humans would have gotten hurt in the fall to the temple floor.

30
00:02:00.224 --> 00:02:03.347
But Mowgli fell exactly as Baloo had taught him.

31
00:02:04.347 --> 00:02:05.888
He landed on his feet.

32
00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.052
"Stay in there," a monkey said.

33
00:02:10.072 --> 00:02:13.334
"We'll be back after we get rid of your friend!"

34
00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:17.377
Now Mowgli could hear Kaa.

35
00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:20.880
He quickly gave the snake's call.

36
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.722
There were other snakes inside the ruins.

37
00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:25.884
They hissed back at him.

38
00:02:28.104 --> 00:02:30.285
"Stand still, Little Brother.

39
00:02:30.305 --> 00:02:32.845
Please don't step on us!"

40
00:02:36.626 --> 00:02:40.308
Mowgli stood as quietly as he could, peering through a hole.

41
00:02:41.428 --> 00:02:44.469
He listened to the furious sound of Bagheera fighting.

42
00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:48.390
"Baloo must be here too," Mowgli thought.

43
00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.151
Bagheera would not have come without him.

44
00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:55.372
"But right now Bagheera could use some help from me."

45
00:02:56.536 --> 00:02:59.357
"Go to the water tank, Bagheera," he shouted.

46
00:02:59.377 --> 00:03:01.497
"Get to the water!"

47
00:03:02.418 --> 00:03:04.238
Bagheera heard Mowgli's cry.

48
00:03:04.258 --> 00:03:06.619
"Thank goodness!"

49
00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.860
the panther thought, fighting his way toward the tanks.

50
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.600
"The man cub is safe!"

51
00:03:13.561 --> 00:03:15.161
Suddenly a shout rose.

52
00:03:16.241 --> 00:03:17.022
It was Baloo.

53
00:03:17.042 --> 00:03:20.162
"Bagheera! I'm here!"

54
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:25.024
The old bear panted as he climbed the terrace.

55
00:03:30.727 --> 00:03:34.809
He threw himself onto his rear legs and held out his paws.

56
00:03:35.649 --> 00:03:38.291
Then he began to hit away monkeys.

57
00:03:38.711 --> 00:03:43.974
Bat-bat-bat! Mowgli heard a crash, followed by a splash.

58
00:03:44.974 --> 00:03:47.256
Bagheera had made it to the water tank!

59
00:03:47.996 --> 00:03:50.297
The monkeys would not follow him in there.

60
00:03:51.178 --> 00:03:55.060
The panther gasped for breath, his head just out of the water.

61
00:03:56.176 --> 00:04:00.038
Monkeys stood on the steps, dancing up and down with rage.

62
00:04:01.838 --> 00:04:05.520
They were ready to spring on him when he came out to help Baloo.

63
00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.741
"Where's Kaa?"

64
00:04:08.021 --> 00:04:08.841
Bagheera thought.

65
00:04:09.742 --> 00:04:10.902
Had the snake left?

66
00:04:12.103 --> 00:04:15.844
He lifted his dripping chin and gave the snake's call.

67
00:04:18.285 --> 00:04:22.187
It had taken Kaa a long time to get over the west wall.

68
00:04:23.347 --> 00:04:29.522
He coiled and uncoiled himself, to be sure that every bit of his long body was working.

69
00:04:31.863 --> 00:04:34.364
Meanwhile, Baloo fought some monkeys.

70
00:04:36.024 --> 00:04:41.147
Mang the bat flew back and forth over them all, carrying the news of the battle.

71
00:04:43.027 --> 00:04:48.850
Then Hathi the elephant trumpeted loudly, waking up birds and more monkeys.

72
00:04:50.331 --> 00:04:53.552
Jungle animals began racing toward Monkey City.

73
00:04:54.912 --> 00:04:59.094
All at once Kaa came—ready to deliver a crushing blow.

74
00:05:00.314 --> 00:05:04.696
The python's first strike drove into the heart of the crowd around Baloo.

75
00:05:05.817 --> 00:05:07.417
He didn't need to strike again.

76
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:11.159
For all at once the monkeys scattered.

77
00:05:11.179 --> 00:05:15.300
"It's Kaa!"

78
00:05:15.521 --> 00:05:16.201
they cried.

79
00:05:16.221 --> 00:05:18.362
"Run!"
